  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"Near-isotropic, reconstructed volume electron microscopy (FIB-SEM) of P7 mouse pancreas\" has been cited 11 times, indicating a measurable academic uptake. Furthermore, it has evidenced diverse downstream reuse, with a total of 12 citations linked to associated works.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in 2023 and available as an open-access dataset, this work contributes valuable insights into the structural and functional assessments of the pancreas using advanced microscopy techniques. Despite limited online outreach, the scholarly community has recognized its significance, with a notable citation count demonstrating its relevance in related fields.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">The data has facilitated discussions and further research, indicated by its reuse in both preprints and associated articles. Notably, it has been referenced in a preprint focusing on the structural and interaction dynamics of beta cell primary cilia, underscoring its interdisciplinary impact across cell biology and pathology.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset features advanced methodologies involving glutaraldehyde fixation and scanning electron microscopy, positioning it at the intersection of biomedical engineering and anatomy studies. Researchers have been able to leverage this dataset in a variety of contexts, enhancing the exploration of pancreatic biology.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">As a product of the Janelia Research Campus, the research reflects on the collaboration within the CellMap Project, involving various contributors dedicated to advancing methods in volumetric imaging. Future efforts to increase visibility and uptake could bolster its integration into teaching resources and further scientific discourse.</p>",
